# How much of the world's plastic waste gets recycled?
subtitle: "Split the world's plastic waste between recycling, burning, landfill and litter, then see the real share recycled and why it rarely lasts."
tags: ["earth","chemistry","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Into the recycling bin. Then?\" note \"?%\" card wood eyes"
voices: {"a":"gemini:Schedar | an even, thoughtful data-journalist quiz host; calm, natural pace","take":"lines"}

## How much of the world's plastic waste gets recycled?
affirm: playful
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Recycled
      - Burned
      - Mismanaged
      - Landfill
    values:
      - 9
      - 19
      - 23
      - 49
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 100
    y_label: '% of plastic waste'
    bar_colors: each
    label_size: 30
    icons:
      - {of: recycling symbol, set: twemoji}
      - {of: fire, set: twemoji}
      - {of: no littering, set: twemoji}
      - {of: hole, set: twemoji}
sources:
    - id: fate
      title: Annual plastic waste by disposal method (World, 2019)
      authors: Our World in Data, from OECD Global Plastics Outlook (2022)
      year: 2022
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/global-plastic-fate
      finding: '2019: recycled 32.8 Mt, incinerated 67.3 Mt, mismanaged/littered 79.3 Mt, landfilled 173.8 Mt of about 353 Mt: 9% recycled, 19% burned, 22% mismanaged, 49% landfilled'
    - id: faq
      title: FAQs on plastics
      authors: Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data)
      year: 2023
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/faq-on-plastics
      finding: of the plastic recycled to date, only 10 percent has been recycled more than once (Geyer et al. 2017); processing degrades the material; 'recycling delays, rather than avoids, final disposal'

