    card title "How much plastic gets recycled?"

Of all the plastic the world throws away, about three hundred and fifty million tonnes a year, how much actually gets recycled?
    draw axes tonnes

    ask "Split 100 percent between the four bars, then press Done." on all budget 100 account_label Left store g default 40,15,10,35
        right: Close. Your split is near the real one.
        wrong: The real split is less kind to recycling.

Recycled: about nine percent. Fewer than one piece in ten.
    highlight bar_1

Half goes into landfill, and a fifth is burned.
    highlight bar_4 bar_2

And over a fifth is mismanaged: dumped, burned in open pits or left to blow away. That's the plastic that can reach rivers and the sea.
    highlight bar_3

    erase axes bar_1 bar_2 bar_3 bar_4 tonnes

But here's the twist. Of every hundred pieces thrown out, nine get recycled.
    draw s100 n100 w100 a1 s9 n9 w9

And of all plastic ever recycled, only about one in ten has been recycled a second time. So: about one piece in a hundred.
    draw a2 s1 n1 w1

Each melt weakens it, so most recycled plastic becomes something lower-grade, and then waste. Recycling delays the bin more than it avoids it.
    highlight s9

So recycle what you can, but the plastic that never ends up anywhere is the plastic never made.
    text never "best: never made" #b5482e x 720 y 560 font_size 56

